==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|day of doom|domesday||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|domes}} + {{m|enm|dai}}, from {{inh|en|ang|dom||judgment}} + {{m|ang|dæg||day}}. Equivalent to {{affix|en|doom|-s-|day}}. Possibly influenced by [[Latin]] {{m|la|domus dei|t=house of God}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈduːmz.deɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-doomsday.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|dooms|day}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The day when [[God]] is expected to judge the [[world]]; the [[end times]].
# [[judgement day|Judgement day]]; the day of the [[Final Judgment]]; any day of decisive judgement or final dissolution.

